1
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:10,080
THE CHARACTERS, RACES,
AND LOCATIONS ARE FICTIONAL.

2
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:12,720
THE HISTORY OF MINORITY STRUGGLES IS REAL.

3
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:58,400
What's it gonna be, you scum?
Come take a swing at me.

4
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:03,640
Looks like I might have
to stay here for a while.

5
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:05,120
Irene.

6
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:08,320
Chart!

7
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:14,160
Kase warriors never die!

8
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:18,960
Mintada!

9
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:22,200
Alright.

10
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:24,240
I'll speak to her for you.

11
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:26,120
Thanks a lot.

12
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:27,600
Please take care of my boy.

13
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:28,800
Yeah.

14
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:30,240
I'm leaving then.

15
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:51,720
Dad.

16
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:52,960
Who are those two?

17
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:55,640
Village Chief Krajuetoh.

18
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:57,120
He came to ask for your hand.

19
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:58,080
What's my hand for?

20
00:02:58,160 --> 00:03:00,640
Huh! What a strange question.

21
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:03,360
He's not asking
for you to be his mother, is he?

22
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:07,360
He's coming to ask
for you to be his son's wife.

23
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:12,600
-The village chief's son?
-Mm.

24
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:16,040
The one tagging after him everywhere?
He's coming to ask for me as his wife?

25
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:18,240
Yeah, that's the one.

26
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,160
And what did you say?

27
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:23,400
What else could I say?
He came all this way to ask.

28
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:24,960
Dad!

29
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:27,040
Well, that lad.

30
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:30,000
Sure he might not be
a warrior like Colonel Layee

31
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:32,800
but I'll give it to him. He's got guts.

32
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:36,840
He actually had the nerve to ask me
to let him take our fierce tigress

33
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:38,680
of Naka village as his wife.

34
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:39,960
Dad!

35
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:42,040
No! Dad!

36
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:45,440
Ugh.

37
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:48,480
Look at her. Look at her.

38
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,200
Yiaza.

39
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:17,440
Dad, what do you take me for?
Why promise me to someone like that?

40
00:04:17,519 --> 00:04:18,360
Huh?

41
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:20,920
I haven't handed you off to anyone yet.

42
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:25,000
-But you said--
-I haven't given my word to anyone yet.

43
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,240
Yiaza.

44
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:30,640
I'm your father.

45
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:35,880
Why wouldn't I know what's in your heart?

46
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:38,600
My heart?

47
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:44,720
Your heart belongs only to Layee.

48
00:04:50,280 --> 00:04:54,280
But you have to ask yourself.

49
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:59,240
How many more lifetimes
will you spend waiting around for him?

50
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:04,280
When Colonel Layee
is entirely consumed by his warfare,

51
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:06,960
how can you be sure that in his heart

52
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:09,360
there's even a place for you?

53
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:13,160
And how can you
ever be certain that in his heart

54
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:16,280
you are his one and only life partner?

55
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:18,280
Hm?

56
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:27,800
EMERGENCY ROOM

57
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:31,080
Chart, my son.
Listen to your mother for a moment.

58
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:35,040
When you find a good person,

59
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:36,720
don't let that chance slip away.

60
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:38,440
Mom, please.

61
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:41,360
Come on in.

62
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:45,240
It's you.

63
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:55,000
Excuse me.

64
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:57,600
I'm here to clean the wound.

65
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:00,360
Go right ahead.

66
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:02,480
Take all the time you need.

67
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:05,640
Chart was complaining
about the wound stinging.

68
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:07,440
Right?

69
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:08,840
Mom.

70
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:13,200
Please go ahead.

71
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:27,520
You and your mother seem very close.

72
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:28,880
We are.

73
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:31,600
My dad died when I was little.

74
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:34,560
Mom is my whole world

75
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:37,360
and I am hers.

76
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:44,160
Other than your mother
is there no one else in your life?

77
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:47,640
You mean…

78
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:50,400
Exactly how it sounds.

79
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:52,360
A girlfriend?

80
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:57,360
If we're talking about that let's just say

81
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:58,800
there's plenty.

82
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,320
Though all of those were a long time ago.

83
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:09,640
Now I'm completely single,

84
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:13,760
unless someone's
willing to be my girlfriend.

85
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:20,600
And who exactly do you have in mind?

86
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:24,280
The one standing right in front of me.

87
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:39,400
Aunt Mawae, where is Mintada?

88
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:42,280
He's resting in the hut. What do you want?

89
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:44,040
I've come to fetch him for training.

90
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:47,760
Train? My son isn't healed yet.

91
00:07:47,840 --> 00:07:49,040
You expect him to train?

92
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:51,520
Healed or not, he has to go.

93
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:53,680
It's an order from Colonel Layee.

94
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:56,400
Don't use Colonel Layee's name.

95
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:58,040
Get out of here, Yapo.

96
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:00,000
-Or else.
-Mom, don't!

97
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:08,960
Mintada.

98
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:12,400
I'm a warrior. I have to follow orders.

99
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:36,280
Irene.

100
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:38,559
What are you doing out here?

101
00:08:40,480 --> 00:08:41,320
What about you?

102
00:08:42,159 --> 00:08:43,559
Your wounds aren't fully healed.

103
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:47,400
Even if the doctor let you
go home, you still need to recover.

104
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,720
You shouldn't walk around like this.

105
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:51,600
I came looking for you.

106
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:54,040
Why?

107
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:57,640
I brought you a little something.

108
00:08:58,280 --> 00:08:59,760
To thank you,

109
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:02,520
and for the way
I've come to feel about you

110
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:04,600
during my recovery here.

111
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,760
Once you're gone, we may never meet again.

112
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:17,680
I don't know what tomorrow brings

113
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:21,000
or if I'll even
make it back from a mission.

114
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:23,560
But I can tell you this.

115
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:26,120
I want to see
your face every chance I get.

116
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:30,800
And I promise
I'll come back to you whenever I can.

117
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:36,120
Please take this gift.

118
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:44,440
Open it.

119
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:48,440
You're awfully bossy, aren't you?

120
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:08,520
It's so beautiful.

121
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:11,440
Let me put it on.

122
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:49,040
That's my boy.

123
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:15,240
Go. Fall in.

124
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:18,680
Yapo,

125
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:20,800
you've crossed the line.

126
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:23,040
You can't just do whatever you want.

127
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:24,600
Siprai.

128
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:28,040
Minthada's been down with fever for days.
Have you still not had your fill?

129
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:29,440
Enough, Siprai.

130
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,920
I'm the one who ordered Mintada here.

131
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,920
If you have a problem, take it up with me.

132
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:58,920
Everyone, get down!

133
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,680
Mintada, you holding up?

134
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:16,120
I'm fine.

135
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:21,680
Today we will train for endurance.

136
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:24,120
A Kase warrior must be
able to withstand any condition.

137
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:26,800
No matter how hot or cold,

138
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:31,120
starving, or how excruciating
the pain might be.

139
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,000
I'm so glad
we get to work together again man.

140
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:45,880
The top two of our cohort
joining forces is going to be wild.

141
00:12:46,920 --> 00:12:49,240
Yeah, that's what I was thinking too.

142
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:51,840
But what about you, Chart?

143
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:54,320
All healed up and ready to roll again?

144
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:56,120
Ready or not, wanna find out?

145
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:57,520
I would pass.

146
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:00,040
I don't pick on injured guys.

147
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:01,160
Wow.

148
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:04,240
If it was me,
I wouldn't take that sitting down man.

149
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:08,120
How about this? Ten laps around the field.

150
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:10,880
Loser has to call the winner "boss."

151
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:16,000
You're on, kiddo.

152
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:31,920
Yeah! Let's go!

153
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:34,000
-Up for it?
-Come on!

154
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:35,560
Ready?

155
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,240
Go.

156
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:54,240
-Yeah!
-Go, go!

157
00:14:04,120 --> 00:14:05,520
Carry on.

158
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:09,640
What are they doing?

159
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:16,360
Hey, Chart. Not tired yet, man?

160
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,920
-Not even close.
-Huh?

161
00:14:21,720 --> 00:14:23,600
Keep pushing!

162
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:32,760
Hurry, hurry! Move it, move it!

163
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:34,520
Yeah!

164
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:37,640
Yeah!

165
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:02,640
I'm cooked!

166
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:10,000
Hey.

167
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:13,320
Mintada.

168
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:25,760
There are still many trials ahead
that Kase warriors must train for

169
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:27,880
and overcome.

170
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:30,960
Go home and prep for tomorrow.

171
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:33,280
Dismissed for today.

172
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:36,640
Let's go.

173
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:45,520
Aunt Mawae! Mintada's back!

174
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:47,800
-Mintada. Mintada.
-Mintada.

175
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:49,240
-Bring him in.
-Mintada.

176
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,600
Sit him down first.

177
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:52,000
-Go.
-Come on.

178
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:53,560
-How are you?
-Easy.

179
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:55,240
Sit, Mintada.

180
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:57,120
-Sit.
-How are you feeling, my boy?

181
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,440
Mintada.

182
00:15:59,480 --> 00:16:00,560
Are you okay?

183
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:03,200
He's burning hot! He must have a fever.

184
00:16:04,680 --> 00:16:05,800
My boy.

185
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:11,400
That damn Yapo.
This is all because of him.

186
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:13,640
No.

187
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:16,280
It's me

188
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,040
who needs to be stronger.

189
00:16:22,120 --> 00:16:23,160
Mintada…

190
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:56,320
<i>Fight! Go!</i>

191
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:17,760
Get him!

192
00:17:24,119 --> 00:17:25,599
Yeah!

193
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:35,280
I'm fine.

194
00:17:58,760 --> 00:17:59,600
All done.

195
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:01,800
Thanks.

196
00:18:04,520 --> 00:18:06,360
-Colonel.
-What?

197
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:09,920
I've received word that Sawin
troops are patrolling near our borders.

198
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:11,720
What do they want?

199
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:13,160
I don't know yet,

200
00:18:13,240 --> 00:18:15,440
but I have our scouts
keeping an eye on them.

201
00:18:15,520 --> 00:18:16,520
Good.

202
00:18:17,040 --> 00:18:19,800
The moment they step
across our border, wipe them out.

203
00:18:19,880 --> 00:18:21,080
Understood.

204
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:42,880
Yiaza.

205
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:44,560
Done with the drills?

206
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:46,160
Not yet.

207
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:49,200
Right now I have to push everyone harder.

208
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:50,760
We have to prepare.

209
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:53,600
Once the rainy season ends,
the Sawin forces will hit us hard.

210
00:18:54,360 --> 00:18:57,520
War is the only thing
that gets you to talk.

211
00:18:58,120 --> 00:19:01,240
Every breath you take is war.

212
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:07,000
Why such a heavy sigh?
Are you not feeling well?

213
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:10,720
The son of the Krajuetoh village head
came asking to make me his wife.

214
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:12,680
And what did you answer?

215
00:19:12,760 --> 00:19:14,680
What did you want me to say?

216
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,160
Dad.

217
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:40,360
I've made up my mind.
I'm going to ask for Yiaza's hand.

218
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:42,360
Really?

219
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:45,360
I have seen you sing love songs for Yieza

220
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:47,200
through countless winters.

221
00:19:47,880 --> 00:19:49,200
Singing again and again.

222
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:52,320
Yet seeing nothing come of it.

223
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:55,280
I thought your affection
for her had long since faded.

224
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:58,400
What are you talking about?
I love Yiaza to death.

225
00:19:58,480 --> 00:20:00,000
But I couldn't act on it

226
00:20:00,080 --> 00:20:02,400
because war has
always been weighing on my mind.

227
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:03,680
So why now?

228
00:20:04,280 --> 00:20:07,920
What made you suddenly
decide to take Yiaza as your wife?

229
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,960
Because a man from
another village is coming to ask for her.

230
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:13,720
So you've got a rival.

231
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:21,080
Are you absolutely sure
you're ready for a wife?

232
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:24,080
I'm sure. Yiaza will make a great wife

233
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:26,720
because she understands
the heart of a warrior like me.

234
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:30,280
Being together won't stop me
from giving everything to battle.

235
00:20:30,360 --> 00:20:33,320
You're being far
too selfish, Colonel Layee.

236
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:39,080
Dad.

237
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:45,880
How am I being selfish?

238
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:48,800
All you care about is war

239
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:51,480
without a single thought
for the heart of your future wife.

240
00:20:51,560 --> 00:20:55,120
In our Kase tribe,
a husband and wife are equals.

241
00:20:55,720 --> 00:20:57,880
It is not for
the husband to do as he pleases

242
00:20:57,960 --> 00:21:00,400
while leaving the wife
to simply endure it.

243
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:02,480
You say you love Yiaza

244
00:21:03,440 --> 00:21:05,520
but what have you ever done for her?

245
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:13,120
If your mind's still cloudy

246
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:14,840
go to the Mirror Pond.

247
00:21:15,600 --> 00:21:16,960
Throw in a stone.

248
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:20,120
Watch the water
and then come back and tell me

249
00:21:20,840 --> 00:21:22,280
what you see.

250
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:46,360
Dad. Dad.

251
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:51,800
Dad, I got it.

252
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:53,520
Is that so?

253
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:57,800
-Your head cleared up already?
-Yes.

254
00:21:58,680 --> 00:22:01,960
You and the Mirror Pond
brought me to my senses. Thanks, Dad.

255
00:22:02,040 --> 00:22:03,520
Don't thank me.

256
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:05,680
Go thank the one with the unwavering heart

257
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:08,760
who loved and waited only for you.

258
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,760
Dad, I'm going to do the laundry.

259
00:22:44,240 --> 00:22:45,960
What are you doing here?

260
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:47,400
I've come for an answer.

261
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:48,720
An answer to what?

262
00:22:48,800 --> 00:22:50,080
To what lies in your heart.

263
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:53,840
I have no answer for you.

264
00:22:53,920 --> 00:22:56,400
I do. Come with me.

265
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:58,480
Where? Where are you taking me?

266
00:22:58,560 --> 00:22:59,800
To the Mirror Pond.

267
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:01,080
Why there?

268
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:02,720
You’ll see when we get there.

269
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:22,880
Before my father and mother got married,

270
00:23:23,480 --> 00:23:25,720
they came to the Mirror Pond like this.

271
00:23:27,680 --> 00:23:31,840
And they were married,
living happily together ever after.

272
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:34,760
Yes.

273
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:38,320
Just like every young
Kase couple who comes here.

274
00:23:39,120 --> 00:23:43,360
Each receives the blessing
of the Pond, to find fulfillment in love.

275
00:23:46,360 --> 00:23:48,840
And what do you want to tell me?

276
00:23:50,520 --> 00:23:52,040
I want to thank you.

277
00:23:54,160 --> 00:23:55,480
Thank me?

278
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:57,840
For what?

279
00:23:57,920 --> 00:23:59,720
For waiting for me all this time.

280
00:24:01,320 --> 00:24:02,800
Waiting for you?

281
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:07,480
Yiaza.

282
00:24:08,920 --> 00:24:10,200
I love you.

283
00:24:10,840 --> 00:24:13,760
Not just because you
let me fight as a brave warrior

284
00:24:13,840 --> 00:24:15,880
but for the spirit within you.

285
00:24:16,800 --> 00:24:19,880
So pure and calm
like the waters of the Mirror Pond.

286
00:24:21,360 --> 00:24:23,160
No matter what ripples disturb your heart.

287
00:24:23,880 --> 00:24:26,840
Before long, your heart
finds its way back to quiet serenity.

288
00:24:28,920 --> 00:24:30,680
You are unshaken by anything,

289
00:24:31,560 --> 00:24:34,240
unchanging with the passage of time.

290
00:24:39,560 --> 00:24:41,320
If I marry you

291
00:24:42,480 --> 00:24:44,080
I promise never to make you sad.

292
00:24:44,600 --> 00:24:45,520
I swear it.

293
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:48,400
Are you finished?

294
00:24:48,480 --> 00:24:50,000
I am.

295
00:25:15,720 --> 00:25:17,640
-Sa.
-Your friends.

296
00:25:17,720 --> 00:25:19,160
-Forgot about us?
-Sorry.

297
00:25:19,240 --> 00:25:20,520
Sorry.

298
00:25:21,640 --> 00:25:22,720
You're so cruel.

299
00:25:22,800 --> 00:25:24,920
We barely made it out.

300
00:25:26,760 --> 00:25:28,120
It's huge, Sa.

301
00:25:28,200 --> 00:25:29,560
I know, right?

302
00:25:30,360 --> 00:25:31,480
Wow.

303
00:25:32,480 --> 00:25:33,400
Is it beautiful, kids?

304
00:25:33,480 --> 00:25:35,760
It's gorgeous, Dad. I love it.

305
00:25:35,840 --> 00:25:38,960
Sa, shall we all take a walk around?

306
00:25:39,040 --> 00:25:40,560
-Shall we?
-Sounds great.

307
00:25:40,640 --> 00:25:42,360
Allow me to show you around.

308
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:44,920
-Chart!
-Oh?

309
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:47,440
-Hello, Uncle Pipach, Aunt Pisinee.
-Hello.

310
00:25:48,200 --> 00:25:49,040
Been waiting long?

311
00:25:49,120 --> 00:25:51,200
I heard you were coming,

312
00:25:51,280 --> 00:25:52,240
so I came by.

313
00:25:56,880 --> 00:25:59,040
Hello, Chart.

314
00:25:59,120 --> 00:26:01,040
Oh, the whole crew is here.

315
00:26:02,040 --> 00:26:05,160
We actually came here
specifically to see you.

316
00:26:05,240 --> 00:26:06,080
To see me?

317
00:26:07,280 --> 00:26:08,400
What are you girls up to?

318
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:11,920
Well, these girls had a stroke of genius.

319
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:14,560
They want you to tutor them for the exam.

320
00:26:15,880 --> 00:26:17,200
Me? I can't tutor anyone.

321
00:26:17,280 --> 00:26:19,200
Why couldn't you, Chart?

322
00:26:19,280 --> 00:26:22,440
If it weren't for you all through school,

323
00:26:22,520 --> 00:26:25,760
I don't know if I'd have made it this far.

324
00:26:25,840 --> 00:26:27,360
-Right?
-Yeah.

325
00:26:27,880 --> 00:26:29,720
-Please, Brother.
-Chart.

326
00:26:29,800 --> 00:26:31,040
-Please.
-Please, Chart.

327
00:26:31,120 --> 00:26:33,800
-Pretty please.
-Tutor us, Chart.

328
00:26:33,880 --> 00:26:35,120
Alright. Fine.

329
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:39,560
You are so sweet. I love you
the most in the whole wide world!

330
00:26:39,640 --> 00:26:41,720
Don't try to butter me up now.

331
00:26:41,800 --> 00:26:43,680
Come on. Take a walk around first.

332
00:26:43,760 --> 00:26:45,360
-Sure.
-We'll figure out the tutoring later.

333
00:26:45,440 --> 00:26:47,200
-Yes, sure.
-Let's have fun!

334
00:26:47,280 --> 00:26:48,960
Thanks a lot, Chart.

335
00:26:49,040 --> 00:26:51,800
-I'll leave the girls in your hands then.
-Sure.

336
00:26:53,760 --> 00:26:54,720
-Let's go.
-Yeah.

337
00:26:54,800 --> 00:26:56,400
Can we leave our stuff here?

338
00:26:56,480 --> 00:26:57,600
This is super heavy.

339
00:26:57,680 --> 00:26:58,920
-Leave it.
-In the van.

340
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:00,120
Just leave it in the van.

341
00:27:00,920 --> 00:27:03,200
-Done.
-Whoa.

342
00:27:03,280 --> 00:27:04,520
What's the rush?

343
00:27:07,240 --> 00:27:08,840
First thing, spill the tea right now.

344
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:11,840
How are things with that pretty nurse?

345
00:27:11,920 --> 00:27:13,240
How's it going?

346
00:27:15,480 --> 00:27:16,680
Why are you asking?

347
00:27:17,440 --> 00:27:19,160
Just curious.

348
00:27:19,240 --> 00:27:22,600
Have you already forgotten
what I did for you back then?

349
00:27:25,960 --> 00:27:27,200
Come on, Chart.

350
00:27:27,280 --> 00:27:30,720
You can't be like this. Women like clarity

351
00:27:30,800 --> 00:27:33,600
and commitment. If you're going
to love, you have to go all in.

352
00:27:33,680 --> 00:27:35,680
Make her see you're not playing around!

353
00:27:37,360 --> 00:27:40,840
You talk like you're an adult
who's been around the block.

354
00:27:40,920 --> 00:27:43,000
It’s just sound theory!

355
00:27:44,320 --> 00:27:45,160
Spill it or what?

356
00:27:49,520 --> 00:27:51,240
-Nope.
-Chart.

357
00:27:51,920 --> 00:27:53,720
-Let's go over there.
-Chart.

358
00:27:53,800 --> 00:27:54,880
Just go.

359
00:27:54,960 --> 00:27:57,520
-Not another word.
-Keeping secrets from me now?

360
00:27:57,600 --> 00:27:59,200
How is it? Nice, right?

361
00:27:59,280 --> 00:28:01,280
The air is amazing.

362
00:28:07,880 --> 00:28:08,840
Look.

363
00:28:09,360 --> 00:28:11,120
Across this river

364
00:28:11,200 --> 00:28:13,040
is the Naka Mountain Range.

365
00:28:13,120 --> 00:28:15,480
And if you go beyond those mountains,

366
00:28:16,440 --> 00:28:18,480
everything changes
in ways you wouldn't believe.

367
00:28:20,440 --> 00:28:22,480
Is this the Naka Mountain Range

368
00:28:22,560 --> 00:28:25,040
that marks the border between Thailand

369
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:27,040
and the Sawin Federation?

370
00:28:27,640 --> 00:28:28,920
In a way, yes.

371
00:28:29,840 --> 00:28:30,840
Or maybe not.

372
00:28:32,360 --> 00:28:34,320
Truth is that land

373
00:28:34,400 --> 00:28:36,320
belongs to the Kase ethnic group.

374
00:28:37,720 --> 00:28:40,040
The Kases governed themselves
for a long time

375
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:43,240
until the Sawin government
refused to recognize them

376
00:28:44,360 --> 00:28:46,720
and waged war to seize the land.

377
00:28:47,680 --> 00:28:51,160
Why is the Sawin government
so eager to take that land?

378
00:28:52,240 --> 00:28:54,720
Sawin claims it's about unity.

379
00:28:55,440 --> 00:28:57,560
But the real reason hidden underneath is

380
00:28:58,360 --> 00:29:00,480
its abundance of natural resources.

381
00:29:03,200 --> 00:29:06,200
The Kases have
protected their forests for generations,

382
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:09,520
making that land enormously valuable.

383
00:29:10,680 --> 00:29:12,360
I see.

384
00:29:13,360 --> 00:29:16,720
People kill each other
over something like that?

385
00:29:21,040 --> 00:29:25,640
<i>Upon the highest land God has called us to</i>

386
00:29:25,720 --> 00:29:30,440
<i>Lies a life of beauty and abundance</i>

387
00:29:30,520 --> 00:29:34,720
<i>May Christ lead my way</i>

388
00:29:34,800 --> 00:29:39,120
<i>I will press on forward</i>

389
00:29:39,200 --> 00:29:43,720
<i>Every day and every night</i>

390
00:29:43,800 --> 00:29:47,880
<i>Moving forward through prayer</i>

391
00:29:47,960 --> 00:29:52,120
<i>Building a bond with God</i>

392
00:29:52,200 --> 00:29:56,560
<i>Press on toward the goal</i>

393
00:29:56,640 --> 00:29:58,640
<i>Lead me to the highest realm</i>

394
00:29:58,720 --> 00:30:00,640
<i>Lead me to the highest realm</i>

395
00:30:00,720 --> 00:30:04,760
<i>Lead me to the highest realm</i>

396
00:30:04,840 --> 00:30:08,920
<i>When I reach that highest land</i>

397
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:13,320
<i>When I reach that highest land</i>

398
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:18,440
<i>I will sing praise Hallelujah</i>

399
00:30:18,520 --> 00:30:24,440
<i>I will sing praise Hallelujah</i>

400
00:31:38,720 --> 00:31:40,160
Come back safe.

401
00:31:55,840 --> 00:31:57,720
This auspicious woven pattern cloth…

402
00:31:58,320 --> 00:31:59,960
I once wove it for your father.

403
00:32:00,480 --> 00:32:03,040
It will bring you victory, my boy.

404
00:32:24,200 --> 00:32:25,720
Thank you, Mom.

405
00:32:26,760 --> 00:32:28,280
Come back victorious, Son.

406
00:33:54,880 --> 00:33:56,000
Load it all up.

407
00:34:20,159 --> 00:34:23,080
EMERGENCY ROOM

408
00:34:33,159 --> 00:34:34,120
What is this?

409
00:34:34,199 --> 00:34:36,159
Hop on. I'm taking you home.

410
00:34:37,040 --> 00:34:39,600
Why give me a ride?
My house is right over there.

411
00:34:39,679 --> 00:34:41,320
That's better.

412
00:34:42,159 --> 00:34:44,800
Gives us time to take the long way around…
through my heart.

413
00:34:48,280 --> 00:34:50,480
No, thanks. I'm way too tired today.

414
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:24,240
You look even more stunning
wearing this necklace.

415
00:35:30,840 --> 00:35:33,880
Are you hungry? Because I'm starving.

416
00:35:36,760 --> 00:35:38,560
Just seeing you makes me full.

417
00:35:39,600 --> 00:35:42,960
Really? Don't let me see
you empty your bowl then.

418
00:35:43,040 --> 00:35:44,360
Hey!

419
00:35:45,040 --> 00:35:46,000
Well,

420
00:35:46,760 --> 00:35:49,440
everything tastes good when I'm with you.

421
00:35:51,680 --> 00:35:52,640
Where'd you learn that?

422
00:35:53,240 --> 00:35:54,280
Secret.

423
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:55,240
Are you blushing?

424
00:35:55,320 --> 00:35:56,760
I am, but I love it.

425
00:35:59,960 --> 00:36:01,160
Make everything taste good?

426
00:36:05,240 --> 00:36:06,200
Irene.

427
00:36:07,560 --> 00:36:08,440
Prapt.

428
00:36:10,520 --> 00:36:11,760
Who the hell is this guy?

429
00:36:12,680 --> 00:36:15,000
-And who are you?
-I'm Irene's boyfriend.

430
00:36:15,600 --> 00:36:17,160
We're through.

431
00:36:17,240 --> 00:36:18,680
I'm not through with you.

432
00:36:18,760 --> 00:36:19,920
-Let's go!
-That hurts.

433
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:21,400
-Let go of her.
-It hurts.

434
00:36:24,880 --> 00:36:26,000
This doesn't concern you.

435
00:36:28,160 --> 00:36:30,120
-What if it does?
-Fine.

436
00:36:30,200 --> 00:36:31,520
No!

437
00:36:33,880 --> 00:36:34,840
Prapt!

438
00:36:40,400 --> 00:36:41,200
Chart, watch out!

439
00:36:46,600 --> 00:36:47,640
Watch out!

440
00:36:50,360 --> 00:36:51,360
-Go to hell!
-Chart!

441
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Look out!

442
00:36:56,120 --> 00:36:59,680
Stay away from Irene,
or you'll regret it forever.

443
00:37:18,560 --> 00:37:19,720
Are you alright?

444
00:37:19,800 --> 00:37:21,080
I'm fine.

445
00:37:49,240 --> 00:37:50,920
I've known him for a long time.

446
00:37:51,520 --> 00:37:53,280
He wasn't like this before.

447
00:37:53,360 --> 00:37:57,240
It might be drugs changing him.

448
00:37:58,920 --> 00:38:00,800
It's like he's possessed
by an evil spirit.

449
00:38:02,280 --> 00:38:04,520
I tried begging him to quit.

450
00:38:06,000 --> 00:38:07,160
He promised he would.

451
00:38:09,080 --> 00:38:11,080
But in the end, he always went back to it.

452
00:38:15,400 --> 00:38:16,680
He doesn't just use drugs.

453
00:38:17,360 --> 00:38:19,400
He profits off them too.

454
00:38:21,520 --> 00:38:22,960
Then it's for the best

455
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:25,440
that you cut him out of your life.

456
00:38:26,560 --> 00:38:28,000
Do you still love him?

457
00:38:28,800 --> 00:38:30,320
Not anymore.

458
00:38:30,400 --> 00:38:32,040
It's just pity now.

459
00:38:32,120 --> 00:38:33,920
I wish that he could

460
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:36,280
go back to being the person he used to be.

461
00:39:24,880 --> 00:39:26,160
Colonel Layee,

462
00:39:27,160 --> 00:39:29,800
do you promise to take Yiaza as your wife,

463
00:39:29,880 --> 00:39:32,080
through times of joy

464
00:39:32,160 --> 00:39:34,640
and sorrow,

465
00:39:34,720 --> 00:39:35,720
to cherish her

466
00:39:36,400 --> 00:39:37,800
until death parts you?

467
00:39:37,880 --> 00:39:40,960
Do you make this vow?

468
00:39:41,480 --> 00:39:42,840
I do.

469
00:39:43,360 --> 00:39:44,600
Yiaza,

470
00:39:44,680 --> 00:39:46,320
do you promise to take Colonel Layee

471
00:39:46,400 --> 00:39:49,440
as your husband,
to honor him, to serve him

472
00:39:49,520 --> 00:39:50,600
through times of health and illness

473
00:39:50,680 --> 00:39:53,640
through joy and hardship,
to care for him until death parts you?

474
00:39:53,720 --> 00:39:56,120
Do you make this vow?

475
00:39:56,800 --> 00:39:58,520
Yes, I do.

476
00:39:58,600 --> 00:39:59,640
Did you all hear that?

477
00:39:59,720 --> 00:40:01,360
No.

478
00:40:01,440 --> 00:40:05,000
Speak up a bit louder. Let's do it
one more time. Do you make this vow?

479
00:40:05,080 --> 00:40:07,000
Yes, I do.

480
00:40:07,080 --> 00:40:08,200
Did you hear that?

481
00:40:08,280 --> 00:40:10,040
We still didn't hear it.

482
00:40:10,120 --> 00:40:12,320
You need to say it louder.

483
00:40:12,400 --> 00:40:13,640
Do you make this vow?

484
00:40:13,720 --> 00:40:15,320
Yes, I do!

485
00:40:15,400 --> 00:40:17,400
We heard it!

486
00:40:17,480 --> 00:40:20,560
Since you both have made
your vows before humanity and before God,

487
00:40:20,640 --> 00:40:22,480
what God has joined together,

488
00:40:22,560 --> 00:40:24,520
let no one put asunder.

489
00:40:24,600 --> 00:40:30,000
You two are now of one flesh,

490
00:40:30,080 --> 00:40:31,960
fully husband and wife.

491
00:40:32,040 --> 00:40:34,440
May God bless you both.

492
00:40:34,520 --> 00:40:35,440
Amen.

493
00:40:35,520 --> 00:40:36,560
Yeah!

494
00:41:28,160 --> 00:41:31,840
<i>-Brothers and sisters</i>
<i>-Brothers and sisters</i>

495
00:41:31,920 --> 00:41:35,720
<i>-Brothers and sisters</i>
<i>-Brothers and sisters</i>

496
00:41:35,800 --> 00:41:40,680
<i>We eat fish, we protect the stream</i>
<i>Protect it, yes, protect it</i>

497
00:41:40,760 --> 00:41:45,720
<i>We eat frogs, we guard the cliff</i>
<i>Guard the cliff, yes, guard the cliff</i>

498
00:41:45,800 --> 00:41:49,040
<i>Do not admire, do not envy</i>

499
00:41:49,120 --> 00:41:53,440
<i>Even if the house is good, it's bought</i>
<i>Even if the water is good, it's paid for</i>

500
00:41:53,520 --> 00:41:55,520
<i>Come back to revive our homeland</i>

501
00:41:55,600 --> 00:41:59,520
<i>Just enough clothes to wear</i>
<i>Just enough rice to eat</i>

502
00:42:31,840 --> 00:42:34,520
<i>Gazing at the stars</i>

503
00:42:34,600 --> 00:42:37,360
<i>Pounding rice in the distant sky</i>

504
00:42:37,440 --> 00:42:42,320
<i>I wish I could fly to you</i>
<i>But it's only a dream</i>

505
00:42:43,040 --> 00:42:45,520
<i>Gazing at the stars</i>

506
00:42:45,600 --> 00:42:48,480
<i>Cooking rice in the distant sky</i>

507
00:42:48,560 --> 00:42:53,400
<i>I long to dine</i>
<i>Under the starlight with you</i>

508
00:42:54,640 --> 00:42:57,240
<i>The stars are warmth</i>
<i>A bond of friendship</i>

509
00:42:57,320 --> 00:43:00,320
<i>And a cherished memory</i>

510
00:43:01,400 --> 00:43:07,920
<i>Yet your dreams and life</i>
<i>Belong somewhere I can never reach</i>

511
00:43:09,440 --> 00:43:10,800
<i>I am merely</i>

512
00:43:10,880 --> 00:43:15,280
<i>A cricket tied to the soil and the roots</i>

513
00:43:16,240 --> 00:43:22,920
<i>My dreams and my destiny</i>
<i>Have driven a wedge between us</i>

514
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:29,480
<i>Ideals borne upon my shoulders</i>

515
00:43:30,840 --> 00:43:35,840
<i>Tied to the motherland</i>

516
00:43:35,920 --> 00:43:41,600
<i>For our kin, to claim our liberty</i>

517
00:43:41,680 --> 00:43:46,360
<i>I need to reclaim my home</i>

518
00:43:47,600 --> 00:43:48,640
How lovely

519
00:43:49,240 --> 00:43:51,560
to have a happy occasion
to enjoy ourselves

520
00:43:51,640 --> 00:43:53,600
and warm our hearts.

521
00:43:54,320 --> 00:43:55,160
Indeed.

522
00:43:55,760 --> 00:43:58,920
If we had only good things
and never had to think of war,

523
00:43:59,000 --> 00:44:00,720
life would be truly happy.

524
00:44:01,880 --> 00:44:04,800
I wonder how long before we reach that day

525
00:44:04,880 --> 00:44:06,880
when our motherland is finally at peace.

526
00:44:08,440 --> 00:44:10,280
Divided by mere rivers and mountains,

527
00:44:10,800 --> 00:44:12,720
Thailand prospers,

528
00:44:12,800 --> 00:44:14,840
its people living in freedom.

529
00:44:15,760 --> 00:44:17,400
A stark contrast to our lives.

530
00:44:23,440 --> 00:44:25,800
When will Kase ever know such happiness?

531
00:44:26,840 --> 00:44:30,440
<i>Please cast your light and guide my path</i>

532
00:44:30,520 --> 00:44:33,240
<i>When my grandma and grandpa return</i>

533
00:44:33,320 --> 00:44:38,400
<i>I’ll offer dried fish as my gratitude</i>

534
00:44:45,440 --> 00:44:49,200
You have both paid
respect to the ancestors

535
00:44:49,800 --> 00:44:51,000
and the forest spirits.

536
00:44:52,080 --> 00:44:55,000
Now pay homage to the household spirits.

537
00:45:01,320 --> 00:45:04,960
Now you two
are officially husband and wife.

538
00:45:06,160 --> 00:45:07,680
Let's go, Granny.

539
00:45:10,440 --> 00:45:12,280
Let's leave them to start making babies.

540
00:45:21,640 --> 00:45:22,600
I'll close the door.

541
00:45:41,000 --> 00:45:43,840
Weddings have so many rituals.

542
00:45:44,720 --> 00:45:48,240
Honestly combat drills are way easier.

543
00:45:55,960 --> 00:45:57,200
Are you tired?

544
00:46:05,920 --> 00:46:06,960
And…

545
00:46:08,480 --> 00:46:09,320
are you hungry?

546
00:46:09,400 --> 00:46:12,000
I haven't seen you touch any food all day.

547
00:46:15,600 --> 00:46:18,480
Or are you hot? Want to bathe?

548
00:46:18,560 --> 00:46:20,360
I can go fetch some water for you.

549
00:46:20,880 --> 00:46:23,120
What are you laughing at, Yiaza?

550
00:46:24,440 --> 00:46:25,800
You know…

551
00:46:26,840 --> 00:46:28,360
I'm no good with words.

552
00:46:29,840 --> 00:46:32,480
Then say no more.

553
00:46:35,720 --> 00:46:38,200
All I know is how to fight, you know that.

554
00:46:43,520 --> 00:46:45,280
I'm so glad

555
00:46:46,720 --> 00:46:48,480
I got to marry you.

556
00:46:49,720 --> 00:46:51,160
I'm happier still.

557
00:46:52,600 --> 00:46:56,080
And I want to thank you so much

558
00:46:57,520 --> 00:46:59,240
for marrying me willingly.

559
00:47:01,800 --> 00:47:05,400
I've never loved anyone but you.

560
00:47:08,480 --> 00:47:10,640
I love you, Yiaza.

561
00:47:43,200 --> 00:47:45,680
How did the entrance exam go?

562
00:47:47,760 --> 00:47:51,240
Well I "finished" it…
now I just hope I didn't finish myself.

563
00:47:51,320 --> 00:47:53,280
You've got this.

564
00:47:53,360 --> 00:47:55,600
You're my sister.
You're the absolute best.

565
00:47:57,200 --> 00:47:59,680
It's only because I had a good tutor.

566
00:48:03,000 --> 00:48:05,480
But even if I pass the exam,

567
00:48:05,560 --> 00:48:07,800
I still won't get to study
what I actually want.

568
00:48:09,520 --> 00:48:10,800
I understand.

569
00:48:11,680 --> 00:48:14,720
But sometimes we don't get to choose.
You want to be a teacher,

570
00:48:14,800 --> 00:48:17,440
but your father
wants you to study business

571
00:48:17,520 --> 00:48:19,040
so you can take over his company.

572
00:48:19,640 --> 00:48:20,680
Yes.

573
00:48:22,000 --> 00:48:23,960
But I'm not giving up on my dream.

574
00:48:24,960 --> 00:48:27,760
For now I'll do what Dad wants.

575
00:48:28,280 --> 00:48:29,560
I'll do it for him.

576
00:48:30,120 --> 00:48:31,480
When the day comes,

577
00:48:32,360 --> 00:48:33,920
I'm going to follow my own path.

578
00:48:34,000 --> 00:48:37,800
That’s my girl.
Meeting in the middle is much better than

579
00:48:37,880 --> 00:48:39,400
stubbornly pushing for your own way.

580
00:48:40,160 --> 00:48:41,080
Good job.

581
00:48:43,800 --> 00:48:44,640
Chart.

582
00:48:47,000 --> 00:48:47,840
Oh, Irene.

583
00:48:50,760 --> 00:48:51,680
Hello.

584
00:48:51,760 --> 00:48:52,880
Hello.

585
00:48:54,920 --> 00:48:56,440
Have you been here long, Punpussa?

586
00:48:57,040 --> 00:48:58,800
You can just call me Sa.

587
00:48:59,960 --> 00:49:04,160
I just got here too. Thought I'd unwind
a bit after finishing the exam.

588
00:49:06,960 --> 00:49:08,480
Well, well…

589
00:49:08,560 --> 00:49:10,520
Look who had a surprise!

590
00:49:10,600 --> 00:49:13,040
Kept your sister in the dark, huh?

591
00:49:13,120 --> 00:49:17,960
What can I say? Special trips
are reserved for special people.

592
00:49:20,640 --> 00:49:23,560
This non-special person is starving.

593
00:49:24,200 --> 00:49:25,640
Okay.

594
00:49:25,720 --> 00:49:27,920
Don't worry.
Your handsome chauffeur is on it.

595
00:49:28,440 --> 00:49:29,760
-Let's go.
-Wait a second.

596
00:49:30,360 --> 00:49:31,920
What's wrong?

597
00:49:33,560 --> 00:49:35,360
You have to let me pick the restaurant.

598
00:49:39,160 --> 00:49:40,240
Okay.

599
00:49:41,360 --> 00:49:42,680
How could I forget?

600
00:49:42,760 --> 00:49:46,360
Whenever Chart picks a place,
it's always a disaster.

601
00:49:46,440 --> 00:49:47,840
Stop it, Sa.

602
00:50:05,240 --> 00:50:06,960
Warriors of Kase.

603
00:50:07,040 --> 00:50:09,520
I thank you all
for standing and fighting by my side.

604
00:50:09,600 --> 00:50:11,520
For as long as we stand united,

605
00:50:12,160 --> 00:50:14,840
the Sawin government
will never lay claim to the land,

606
00:50:15,480 --> 00:50:18,200
the waters, and the skies

607
00:50:19,240 --> 00:50:21,800
that the Kases have called home
for thousands of years.

608
00:50:21,880 --> 00:50:24,120
All I ask is your promise.

609
00:50:24,200 --> 00:50:26,520
We lay down our lives for Kase.

610
00:50:26,600 --> 00:50:27,720
For Kase!

611
00:50:27,800 --> 00:50:28,920
For Kase!

612
00:50:29,000 --> 00:50:29,880
For Kase!

613
00:50:29,960 --> 00:50:31,080
For Kase!

614
00:50:31,160 --> 00:50:32,080
For Kase!

615
00:50:32,160 --> 00:50:33,360
For Kase!

616
00:50:36,880 --> 00:50:39,080
Alright. At ease.

617
00:50:39,160 --> 00:50:40,160
Yes, Sir!

618
00:50:43,200 --> 00:50:45,720
Mintada. Siprai.

619
00:50:46,600 --> 00:50:47,760
Follow me.

620
00:50:51,840 --> 00:50:54,440
What did we do wrong to be punished?

621
00:50:54,520 --> 00:50:56,040
Why did you ban us from battle?

622
00:50:56,120 --> 00:50:57,520
This is not punishment.

623
00:50:58,960 --> 00:51:00,240
I have a task for you.

624
00:51:00,320 --> 00:51:01,440
What is the task?

625
00:51:01,520 --> 00:51:02,920
You two must go to Thailand.

626
00:51:03,000 --> 00:51:04,320
Thailand?

627
00:51:09,440 --> 00:51:12,600
A letter from the Kase
National Union Forces arrived yesterday.

628
00:51:13,120 --> 00:51:15,800
Our village has been asked
to select two representatives

629
00:51:15,880 --> 00:51:17,640
to further their studies in Thailand.

630
00:51:19,560 --> 00:51:20,920
Study? Why study?

631
00:51:21,000 --> 00:51:23,040
I don't want to go. I'm staying to fight.

632
00:51:23,120 --> 00:51:24,080
Listen to me.

633
00:51:24,600 --> 00:51:26,680
If we are to protect the land of Kase,

634
00:51:26,760 --> 00:51:28,880
force of arms alone will not be enough.

635
00:51:28,960 --> 00:51:32,600
We need brains just as much as brawn.

636
00:51:34,200 --> 00:51:37,400
That is why
the two of you must go and study.

637
00:51:37,480 --> 00:51:41,920
Acquire the knowledge we need
to rebuild and lead the Kase of tomorrow.

638
00:51:43,280 --> 00:51:45,800
If Colonel believes it will serve Kase

639
00:51:46,440 --> 00:51:48,120
and I am capable of doing it,

640
00:51:48,200 --> 00:51:50,040
I stand ready to do whatever it takes.

641
00:51:51,360 --> 00:51:52,320
What?

642
00:51:53,480 --> 00:51:54,720
What about you, Siprai?

643
00:51:55,320 --> 00:51:56,480
I won't…

644
00:52:03,960 --> 00:52:05,640
I won't refuse.

645
00:52:07,680 --> 00:52:09,360
If Mintada is going,

646
00:52:10,840 --> 00:52:12,040
then I'm going too.

647
00:52:12,560 --> 00:52:15,280
Good. The two of you are my choice.

648
00:52:16,760 --> 00:52:18,760
I have faith in you both.

649
00:52:36,120 --> 00:52:37,560
What's up, little menace?

650
00:52:38,080 --> 00:52:40,360
Guess what!

651
00:52:41,120 --> 00:52:42,200
Can I pass?

652
00:52:43,040 --> 00:52:46,000
I passed the entrance exam
and I got into my first choice!

653
00:52:46,720 --> 00:52:48,840
For real? Sa, that’s huge!

654
00:52:50,040 --> 00:52:52,520
You’re the first person I called.

655
00:52:52,600 --> 00:52:54,600
<i>After all, you were my tutor.</i>

656
00:52:54,680 --> 00:52:56,280
Plus, get this!

657
00:52:56,360 --> 00:52:58,040
Yoon and Nee got in as well.

658
00:52:58,120 --> 00:53:00,720
We're all going to the same uni!

659
00:53:00,800 --> 00:53:02,840
<i>So the three of us are planning</i>

660
00:53:02,920 --> 00:53:05,720
to chip in and treat you
to a thank you meal.

661
00:53:05,800 --> 00:53:07,280
When is good for you?

662
00:53:08,120 --> 00:53:10,720
If you're treating me,
I'm definitely not available.

663
00:53:10,800 --> 00:53:13,000
Huh? Why not?!

664
00:53:13,680 --> 00:53:15,360
If you're treating me, forget it.

665
00:53:15,440 --> 00:53:18,520
But if I get to take you girls
out to celebrate,

666
00:53:18,600 --> 00:53:20,840
start thinking about the place you want.

667
00:53:20,920 --> 00:53:22,800
Wow.

668
00:53:22,880 --> 00:53:25,040
Thank you very much, Chart. Deal.

669
00:53:25,120 --> 00:53:27,360
I’ll tell the girls right away.

670
00:53:27,440 --> 00:53:29,480
They’re gonna scream!

671
00:53:29,560 --> 00:53:32,120
I’ll be waiting, bye.

672
00:53:46,920 --> 00:53:47,800
Siprai.

673
00:53:51,520 --> 00:53:53,400
What are you doing lurking around here?

674
00:53:54,160 --> 00:53:57,280
Or are you waiting to see someone?

675
00:53:59,640 --> 00:54:01,320
Go on your way.

676
00:54:01,400 --> 00:54:03,920
Ah, I see.

677
00:54:04,800 --> 00:54:07,080
You're here for your precious Manu.

678
00:54:07,160 --> 00:54:09,440
Either way, it’s none of your concern.

679
00:54:09,520 --> 00:54:12,280
If so, word of angel advice.

680
00:54:12,360 --> 00:54:14,600
Manu hasn't even showed up this morning.

681
00:54:15,200 --> 00:54:17,680
Then where is she?

682
00:54:17,760 --> 00:54:20,800
Right over there.
At the Colonel Layee's place.

683
00:54:21,320 --> 00:54:22,720
Why? What happened?

684
00:54:22,800 --> 00:54:25,760
Yiaza isn't feeling well.
So Manu dropped by to check on her.

685
00:54:30,480 --> 00:54:32,320
So what exactly is wrong with me?

686
00:54:33,760 --> 00:54:34,960
You're not sick at all.

687
00:54:36,400 --> 00:54:38,240
You're just…

688
00:54:45,360 --> 00:54:46,320
Really?

689
00:54:47,560 --> 00:54:51,320
You were a medic before I was.
You should know well.

690
00:54:52,400 --> 00:54:53,640
I'm not sure.

691
00:54:53,720 --> 00:54:55,320
But I am.

692
00:54:58,360 --> 00:54:59,640
Yiaza.

693
00:55:00,840 --> 00:55:03,040
-Layee.
-Be careful.

694
00:55:03,120 --> 00:55:04,680
I thought you were out on patrol.

695
00:55:04,760 --> 00:55:08,280
I did but I heard you were sick.
So I rushed back.

696
00:55:10,200 --> 00:55:12,200
I should get back to my patients.

697
00:55:38,800 --> 00:55:40,880
Yiaza, what's wrong?

698
00:55:42,880 --> 00:55:44,520
There's something within me,

699
00:55:45,760 --> 00:55:47,880
filling me with such boundless joy.

700
00:55:49,080 --> 00:55:50,240
What is it?

701
00:55:53,880 --> 00:55:57,920
Before long, you will welcome our child.

702
00:55:59,800 --> 00:56:01,320
Are we having a baby?

703
00:56:03,720 --> 00:56:04,720
Yiaza.

704
00:56:18,600 --> 00:56:22,520
Why does it have to be Mintada and Siprai
who get to study abroad in Thailand?

705
00:56:22,600 --> 00:56:23,800
<i>Instead of me!</i>

706
00:56:24,720 --> 00:56:26,880
We won't just sit here
and let them climb right in.

707
00:56:26,960 --> 00:56:28,640
We will never let them

708
00:56:28,720 --> 00:56:30,800
set foot on Thai soil.

709
00:56:30,880 --> 00:56:33,040
Freeze! Put your hands in the air!

710
00:56:37,240 --> 00:56:38,720
No matter how thoroughly we check,

711
00:56:38,800 --> 00:56:42,000
<i>those pests always</i>
<i>find a way to smuggle drugs in.</i>

712
00:56:45,720 --> 00:56:46,760
-Hey! Are you blind?
-Siprai.

713
00:56:46,840 --> 00:56:47,680
Get down here right now!

714
00:56:47,760 --> 00:56:48,960
I'm so sorry.

715
00:57:51,920 --> 00:57:53,800
Subtitle translation by:
Onamon Chaipramote
